00:25:45,070 --> 00:25:54,608
So that is why LiveKit and similar WebRTC implementation provides a service called ICE service or interactive connectivity establishment.

190
00:25:54,768 --> 00:26:02,128
So that means this IC service will actually manage internally whether you need to use a turn service or not, right?

191
00:26:02,286 --> 00:26:03,968
So it will decide itself.

192
00:26:04,048 --> 00:26:17,764
So basically, for a client or an AI agent to communicate, all they have to do is just go through the ICE service, and the IC service knows the best path available to connect to the other client, like the AI agent.

193
00:26:17,968 --> 00:26:30,564
So, for example, in this instance, if the client need to connect with AI agent, the client will go to the IC service and the IC service will basically know how to connect AI agent in a best possible path or in a best possible way.

194
00:26:31,008 --> 00:26:36,516
So it might use the relay if the stun is not available and all these bits.

195
00:26:36,688 --> 00:26:41,476
And if stun is available, it will use stun server and directly connect connect with AI agent.

196
00:26:41,934 --> 00:26:52,868
So as a WebRTC AI agent or as a WebRTC client, if you are designing, you don't have to worry about all this logic about whether to select stun server or turn server.

